# Tracked geodata is pipeline *input*, so it must survive a round trip through
# git byte for byte: a fresh clone has to feed the UI_* tools exactly what the
# originals did. This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise
# rewrite the GeoJSON line endings on checkout — harmless to a parser, but it
# means the working tree no longer holds the bytes that were committed.
Data/JSon-Provinces-Orig/** -text

# Source keeps git's normal handling: LF in the repository, native in the
# working tree.
*.py text
*.md text
